   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ אִיתְּמַר, עֲבוֹדָה זָרָה שֶׁנִּשְׁתַּבְּרָה מֵאֵלֶיהָ. רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן אָמַר: אֲסוּרָה. וְרֵישׁ לָקִישׁ אָמַר: מוּתֶּרֶת.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» Connected with the mishna’s discussion of idol worship it «was stated:» In the case of an object of «idol worship that broke by itself, Rabbi Yoḥanan says:» It is «prohibited» to derive benefit from it, as the fact that it is broken does not constitute nullification, «and Reish Lakish says:» It is «permitted» to derive benefit from it."
  }
